The three core principles (NIST SP 800-207):
Principle	What it means Verify explicitly	Every access request is authenticated and authorised using all available signals (identity, device health, location, behaviour, time, etc.) 
— regardless of where the request comes from. Use least privilege	Grant only the minimum access needed for the specific task, for only as long as it's needed. 
A compromised account can only reach a narrow slice of the environment.
Assume breach	Design security as if attackers are already inside.  The goal shifts from "prevent every intrusion" to limiting blast radius and detecting/responding quickly.

